Translation patch: `value::convert::trusted` (new module: the trust boundary of the value conversions)

Change: Adds `src/value/convert/trusted.rs`, declared `pub(crate) mod trusted` in `convert/mod.rs`: one function per dependency operation that the value conversions use (btoi, regex `is_match`, chrono, time, num-bigint, rust_decimal, bigdecimal, serde_json, and std's UTF-8 checks, `String` bytes, float parsing/widening, integer `to_string`, `Duration`), each body being that single call (`Result`s turned into `Option`s with `.ok()` where callers only test `Ok`/`Err`). The regex statics of `convert/mod.rs` and the format descriptions of `convert/time.rs` are copied here verbatim (patches 41 and 43 remove the originals).
Why: The module is `opaque` in Cargo.toml, so the trusted surface of the value conversions is exactly this list of Rust functions, each with a Lean model or axiom in `FunsExternal.lean`. The dependencies themselves cannot be translated (no MIR for non-inline foreign functions; `LazyLock` statics with closures; float arithmetic; trait-generic numeric code).
Behaviour: Unchanged: the module is not used until the next patches.

